{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors","id":1179894,"title":"Scion Errors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-27T11:56:36-08:00","id":1179894,"title":"Scion Errors","content":"I was looking over the Scion: Origins document sent out to backers today and I think I found a rules error, or maybe I am just not understanding the rule correctly.<br /> <br /> On pg. 105, Skills<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These dots are cumulative for Skills associated with two Paths. If this gives a Skill more than three dots, redistribute the extra dot to another Path Skill. </div> </div> </div>The example given (Little Mao), and the earlier pre-generated characters, have skills above three. Is this an error in the rule or is it when you move dots from overflowing skills you can make a skill go over three dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:11:16-08:00","id":1179896,"title":"","content":"Should be <i>five </i>dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:17:32-08:00","id":1179898,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that is what I assumed.<br /> <br /> I also found that the entire entry for &quot;Larceny&quot;, pg 62, is not in the skills section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2018,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","user":"Bioagent","date":". 01-27-2018, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:19:15-08:00","id":1179899,"title":"","content":"So this is basically the feedback for minor editing errors thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:22:13-08:00","id":1179900,"title":"","content":"I am ok with that.<br /> <br /> PS: I am Alpharius","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:22:48-08:00","id":1179901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1179899#post1179899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is basically the feedback for minor editing errors thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Let's go with what Ian says below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 01-27-2018, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:23:02-08:00","id":1179902,"title":"","content":"There's something up with Step Six of character creation (pp. 107-108). The text says to hand out dots, while the example says it's XP (which comes out to an Attribute dot less than the text).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and in the character creation example for Step Four (p. 106), the character's called Boyd at one point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 01-27-2018, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T12:25:34-08:00","id":1179904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1179899#post1179899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is basically the feedback for minor editing errors thread?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would rather we wait. We'll have a formal errata thread once the fully laid-out backer PDF goes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:32:02-08:00","id":1179939,"title":"","content":"Page 158, last page, first sentence- &quot;It is unsatisfying for most players to think that their characters' stories...&quot; should probably be 'think that *of* their characters' stories.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T14:37:19-08:00","id":1179942,"title":"","content":"I'd say the biggest one is the definition World, The in the lexicon, since it says the gods have only just recently returned and gotten involved in the World rather than, uh, never having left, ever","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T15:24:44-08:00","id":1179951,"title":"","content":"The Deva seem to have Firearms as an Asset Skill instead of Athletics.<br /> <br /> I even went and checked the skill descriptions to make sure Athletics is still the bow-shooting and thrown weapons skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 01-27-2018, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T19:33:30-08:00","id":1180023,"title":"","content":"There are references to a skill called Enigmas but it isn\u2019t in the list of skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T19:43:01-08:00","id":1180026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1179951#post1179951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deva seem to have Firearms as an Asset Skill instead of Athletics.<br /> <br /> I even went and checked the skill descriptions to make sure Athletics is still the bow-shooting and thrown weapons skill.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see the conflict, especially at the Origins level, where characters are generally going to be grounded in a modern context, rather than using historic weapons at mythic levels, making guns the contextual equivalent of historic ranged weapons. I'm inclined to let PCs pick between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T00:47:15-08:00","id":1180093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1180026#post1180026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can see the conflict, especially at the Origins level, where characters are generally going to be grounded in a modern context, rather than using historic weapons at mythic levels, making guns the contextual equivalent of historic ranged weapons. I'm inclined to let PCs pick between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point... would you allow them to change when they Ascend to higher tiers? Not that it technically matters since as I've noted elsewhere Astras don't <i>have</i> to be invoked through bows, and there's no reason they can't be invoked through bullets as easily as arrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T00:48:02-08:00","id":1180094,"title":"","content":"As a separate point, Freyja seems to have Four Callings and Shiva has Epic Strength listed twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T05:29:49-08:00","id":1180130,"title":"","content":"Page 103 mentions Capital-A Aspirations when talking about Deeds; I'm assuming that's what they were originally called since they seem to function similarly to Chronicles of Darkness Aspirations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8871-griffalo","name":"griffalo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8871_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T10:33:23-08:00","id":1180197,"title":"","content":"Page 26, the &quot;Land of Chains&quot; section, second paragraph, second sentence : &quot;They almost possess powerful, implacable, and incorruptible guards.&quot; Should probably be &quot;They almost <i>all</i> possess powerful, implacable, and incorruptible guards.&quot; Or &quot;They almost <i>always</i> possess powerful, implacable, and incorruptible guards.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T18:03:12-08:00","id":1180298,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Repeating this with red text because it seems to have been missed.</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1179904#post1179904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would rather we wait. We'll have a formal errata thread once the fully laid-out backer PDF goes out.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>If people have larger issues of the sort where rules are particularly unclear and preventing them from playing the game, absolutely bring them up: we want you to play, and Neall is happily offering clarifications in those examples.<br /> <br /> However, a full errata of all the nitty-gritty is outside the scope of this thread for now. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T18:38:37-08:00","id":1180310,"title":"","content":"I mentioned it in the PDF release thread, but I'm pretty confused by how the connections rules work, and I haven't seen an explanation elsewhere. It seems like every time you invoke connections to speak to a contact, that contact (Who starts at one dot and one tag) picks up two more dots and tags. Is this correct? Do these persist after the session, or do they reset and just indicate how tied-in that contact is to the current story? Do you need to use invocations to get access (Like, say, would using a detective path to get access to a forensic lab eat one of your invocations, or is that only for calling others in for help?)? I might be confused because I'm missing something, but I'm honestly now sure how to use connections in play.<br /> <br /> Edit: As a followup, I'd kind of like to see an example of access connections for a path or two, because while I can kind of guess that, for a society path of 'Chosen Hero Adopted By Thor' the groups are mythical creatures and worshippers, and the contacts are specific people from the groups, but I've got no idea what kind of practical facilities that would get me access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23646,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23646-goblinsociety","user":"GoblinSociety","date":". 01-28-2018, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23646-goblinsociety","name":"GoblinSociety","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:57:04-08:00","id":1180329,"title":"","content":"Okay, this is something that's really seriously inhibiting my understanding of how the combat rules work...<br /> <br /> It's not totally clear how Injury Conditions are applied. There's this part...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion Origins, Resolving Damage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any time the character takes damage, he must take an Injury Condition. His player chooses to take a Bruised, Injured, or Maimed Condition, if available. If none are available, he is Taken Out.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is pretty clear! Where I get sort of confused is after describing Bruised, Injured and Maimed (while providing examples of the specific Injury Conditions that manifest for each one) we then get to weapon tags, which say stuff like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion Origins, Weapon Tags</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aggravated (2): This weapon deals grievous magical damage, such as a blade made of raw fire or lightning, or the revealed face of a God. Aggravated Injury Conditions are things like Burned Off Completely and Melted Flesh and can only be healed by magical abilities. This is meant expressly for magical and supernatural sources of injury.<br /> <br /> Bashing (0): This weapon deals blunt force damage. The tag allows for the Broken and Battered Injury Conditions. It cannot be used to slice or sever objects (or limbs).<br /> <br /> Lethal (0): The weapon deals lethal damage, which can lead to serious injury. This tag allows for the Scratched, Cut, or Bleeding Out Injury Conditions. A weapon with this tag cannot inflict the Bruised or Battered Injury Conditions</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the idea that a weapon which deals Lethal damage cannot have the player choose to allocate its damage to the Bruised Conditions? Or that Bashing weapons can't afflict more than Bruised Conditions?<br /> <br /> I understand how Defense works now, so this is the last sort of mystery for me, any help is appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T20:57:14-08:00","id":1180334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1180329#post1180329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the idea that a weapon which deals Lethal damage cannot have the player choose to allocate its damage to the Bruised Conditions? Or that Bashing weapons can't afflict more than Bruised Conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is that Lethal and Bashing lead to different Conditions, but not the level? Like the &quot;Scratched&quot; would be the -1 Damage condition for a lethal weapon, &quot;Cut&quot; for -2, and &quot;Bleeding Out&quot; for -4, while the Bashing counterparts would be Bruised, Broken, and Battered. That's how I interpret it, but the wording is kinda confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23784-mexxell","name":"Mexxell","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T04:43:45-08:00","id":1180383,"title":"","content":"I have a general question: It says on pg 119, Knacks, that without a Legend trait anyone with access to supernatural Knacks can only keep one at a time. But pg 107, Step Six: Finishing Touches, says you can get two more Knacks. And just two paragraphs up under Step Five: Calling and Knacks, it says an Origins-level character may only possess one Knack at a time.<br /> <br /> What I get from this is that you can have multiple Knacks, but you'd need to swap out which one is active as a Tweak after a session. The wording seems to contradict a bit, so I'm looking for some clarification here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T05:25:28-08:00","id":1180391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1180383#post1180383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a general question: It says on pg 119, Knacks, that without a Legend trait anyone with access to supernatural Knacks can only keep one at a time. But pg 107, Step Six: Finishing Touches, says you can get two more Knacks. And just two paragraphs up under Step Five: Calling and Knacks, it says an Origins-level character may only possess one Knack at a time.<br /> <br /> What I get from this is that you can have multiple Knacks, but you'd need to swap out which one is active as a Tweak after a session. The wording seems to contradict a bit, so I'm looking for some clarification here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the only way to have more than 1 knack is with &quot;bonus points&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T05:56:40-08:00","id":1180397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1180383#post1180383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a general question: It says on pg 119, Knacks, that without a Legend trait anyone with access to supernatural Knacks can only keep one at a time. But pg 107, Step Six: Finishing Touches, says you can get two more Knacks. And just two paragraphs up under Step Five: Calling and Knacks, it says an Origins-level character may only possess one Knack at a time.<br /> <br /> What I get from this is that you can have multiple Knacks, but you'd need to swap out which one is active as a Tweak after a session. The wording seems to contradict a bit, so I'm looking for some clarification here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall clarified in one of the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179832-makeshift-character-sheet?p=1179895#post1179895\">other threads</a>: Basically, you can have some number of Knacks but only one can be active at a time. You can swap your &quot;active&quot; Knack at the end of the session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T04:46:03-08:00","id":1180664,"title":"","content":"So it doesn't look like you get to add a skill to your dice pool when you Defend. Am I reading that correctly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T05:50:42-08:00","id":1180674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1180664#post1180664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it doesn't look like you get to add a skill to your dice pool when you Defend. Am I reading that correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my read of it. Defence is just straight Attribute (Or 2x Attribute for a Full Defense) <br /> <br /> It strongly rewards [Soft] armour, which is roughly equivalent to 3 extra Defence dice. Take Soft armour any time you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T21:22:40-08:00","id":1181002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GoblinSociety</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1180310#post1180310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned it in the PDF release thread, but I'm pretty confused by how the connections rules work, and I haven't seen an explanation elsewhere. It seems like every time you invoke connections to speak to a contact, that contact (Who starts at one dot and one tag) picks up two more dots and tags. Is this correct? Do these persist after the session, or do they reset and just indicate how tied-in that contact is to the current story? Do you need to use invocations to get access (Like, say, would using a detective path to get access to a forensic lab eat one of your invocations, or is that only for calling others in for help?)? I might be confused because I'm missing something, but I'm honestly now sure how to use connections in play.<br /> <br /> Edit: As a followup, I'd kind of like to see an example of access connections for a path or two, because while I can kind of guess that, for a society path of 'Chosen Hero Adopted By Thor' the groups are mythical creatures and worshippers, and the contacts are specific people from the groups, but I've got no idea what kind of practical facilities that would get me access to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quoting myself because now that the Trinity previews are out, which I believe this was based on, the way contacts work makes even less sense. In Trinity, characters get one contact dot and tag per dot in a path, and increasing a path will be fairly rare. In Scion, invoking paths giving contact dots and tags seems like it would balloon remarkably fast, with a character potentially having a level 3 contact the first time they get in touch with them, and level 5 the next. Is that intentional, or am I misreading how it works in Scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23646,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23646-goblinsociety","user":"GoblinSociety","date":". 01-31-2018, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23646-goblinsociety","name":"GoblinSociety","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:15:28-08:00","id":1181084,"title":"","content":"I have two things that are confusing in their current state. The piercing property references to Armor Value. I assume Armor Value is no longer a thing in the game and that it is a thing from a old version.<br /> <br /> The other, several locations the book asks for you to roll agility and even one time agility and dex. Is this supposed to be Athletics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T06:34:52-08:00","id":1181113,"title":"","content":"Oh yea, something else that I've been wondering even more that I've seen the Deer Women and the Therianthropes. What are the tags for a bareknuckle or hoof style/natural unarmed attack? How are they handled? Do Brass knuckles count as a unarmed attack or just another style of weapon that happens to worn? Id assume going complete bareknuckle may help u with grappling or something but maybe the intent here is that pure unarmed is only used when u have a knack or specific bonus that makes it worthwhile... otherwise its always better to have a weapon.<br /> <br /> Could u possibly give us some insight into this? I know a player of mine is going to want to use pure bareknuckle fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T08:12:25-08:00","id":1181130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1181084#post1181084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have two things that are confusing in their current state. The piercing property references to Armor Value. I assume Armor Value is no longer a thing in the game and that it is a thing from a old version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard 1 and Hard 3 each provide a single extra point of bruised health box, so i assume when it says to reduce armor value by 1, it means to remove one of those boxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T03:00:49-08:00","id":1182527,"title":"","content":"It would be useful to have a character sheet to work with, just to have the right terminology and check that up properly... Because I've seen &quot;resolve&quot; and &quot;intelligence&quot; used plenty of times and we don't know what's going on WITHOUT THE CHARACTER SHEET WHICH IS A BASIS PLEASE <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (this has been asked multiple times all over the place so hopefully you guys will excuse my lack of patience)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23785-vonigner","name":"vonigner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T03:07:05-08:00","id":1182528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonigner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1182527#post1182527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(this has been asked multiple times all over the place so hopefully you guys will excuse my lack of patience)</div> </div> </div> </div>Asking me more than once isn't going to make me go any faster!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T05:06:27-08:00","id":1182549,"title":"","content":"Multiple times over a long-ish period of time, that is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not spamming every second post asking for this basic tool for testing a sytem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23785-vonigner","name":"vonigner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T15:08:25-08:00","id":1182719,"title":"","content":"PLUG! <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hLmk7zfMl-er0v07DvvVfeh5GyCgwvvB_vIAmSiVONU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> (Its a character sheet, albeit a google sheet one based on my own reading of the rules with some extra insights from Neall. Please make your own copy. Post comments and concerns in the &quot;Makeshift Character Sheet&quot; thread.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T22:18:35-08:00","id":1182815,"title":"","content":"Here are some of things that seemed off to me that may not have been mentioned before.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weapon and armor tags</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Piercing should likely reference to soft armor unless ur referring to a different type of defense granted by armor.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Armored Tag? Doesn\u2019t exist.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Versatile states it gives a +1 to any stunts but dealing injuries is actually a stunt. Could be clarified a bit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Kevlar Vest has 4 points of tags instead of 3.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Chainmail has 5 points of tags</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Knacks</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swift Bandage: Is this supposed to heal a -2 condition? Seems like it. Would make sense why it does not list that it can heal hard armor slot injuries considering they are only -1 slots.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Why do some healing abilities state u can heal wounds within hard armor slots but others do not? It seems like a system that should be fairly normalized among all damage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Based on the antagonist section it seems to imply that soft armor is supposed to increase defense directly. Is it supposed to be defense or more successes to do the cause injury stunt?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hard and soft armor seems to be described differently with the super soldier antagonist quality. This is also similar to how soft and hard armor is talked about in the trinity preview. Specifically the assigning the points to hard armor. Is it always 1 point for 1 hard armor and 3 points for 2 or has this system been modified?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Men in Black antagonist have a armor value listed for them. They are the only antagonists that do as far as i can see.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Should birthrights really be listed during origin character creation? The lore heavily implies you only ever receive birthrights after your visitation. That and the fact the paragraph even references to Hero for you to get the information it seems a little odd.<br /> <br /> Anyway, hope that helps. May get time to look through other sections tomorrow.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 02-06-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T06:30:45-08:00","id":1183569,"title":"","content":"The contacts section seems very confusing. I was under the impression that you handled contacts purely by invoking a path and that you could invoke a single path only 1 time per session. One aspect of invoking a path is being about to speak to a contact. It also mentions gaining points every invocation which doesn't make a whole lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T07:51:26-08:00","id":1183588,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't it make more sense for the Seize stunt to require &quot;Variable successes equal to opponent's Might) instead of just 3s? Means big dice pools later on are going to be disarm fests. This makes it harder for a low might person to retain their weapon but that generally makes sense. Low might are either noncombatants or ranged fighters. Both are not being very smart if they are in close range to begin with.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And the Feint stunt seems a bit confusing. Do you want them to spend successes to beat their defense, then spend defense again, and then spend 2 per +1 enhancement they want? Or does it function more like inflict injury but with a cost of 2s instead? In that you spend for their defense and then spend 2 more per enhancement after that. Also, is there a cap to this? Can u actually do damage and then just spend 2 more successes to get a +1 to yourself next turn? Can this even be used on yourself? It would likely need to be in order to work in a solo game. I'm thinking it makes more sense for it to be simply 2s because having to spend double their defense just to begin using the stunt seems off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 02-08-2018, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T12:46:13-08:00","id":1183665,"title":"","content":"I want to make sure I'm understanding defense correctly. When a player is attacked the first time in a round, they roll their Defense stat (highest Resilience, whether that be Stamina, Resolve, or Composure). They can then spend successes on dodge to create a Defense that is what you must hit?<br /> <br /> And if that's right, it says &quot;Enemies have very high defenses to encourage exploiting weaknesses&quot; but most of them only have 1-3 points, same as a player. Do they still roll theirs or is their defense a static value on top of rolling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12919-mystrich","name":"Mystrich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T14:14:50-08:00","id":1183700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mystrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1183665#post1183665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if that's right, it says &amp;quot;Enemies have very high defenses to encourage exploiting weaknesses&amp;quot; but most of them only have 1-3 points, same as a player. Do they still roll theirs or is their defense a static value on top of rolling?</div> </div> </div> </div>My takeaway was that defenses for antagonists are static.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:40:43-07:00","id":1206919,"title":"","content":"Related to the OP, it says on page 104 (second bullet point at the bottom of the page): &quot;Any given skill can be associated with at most two of your paths.&quot; This rule is ignored in the example, which gives Little Mao Culture in all three of his Paths. It also contradicts the point that there might be overflow dots, as five dots is the most you can get from two paths.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>I just reread the middle section of this thread and realized this probably falls into the nitpicking category that has been discouraged. Sorry about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","user":"gscrap","date":". 04-14-2018, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T07:45:51-07:00","id":1209622,"title":"","content":"edit: someone else asked. Will wait for an answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","user":"Gnomeborg","date":". 04-21-2018, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","name":"Gnomeborg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T15:34:36-07:00","id":1209793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179894-scion-errors?p=1206919#post1206919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related to the OP, it says on page 104 (second bullet point at the bottom of the page): &quot;Any given skill can be associated with at most two of your paths.&quot; This rule is ignored in the example, which gives Little Mao Culture in all three of his Paths. It also contradicts the point that there might be overflow dots, as five dots is the most you can get from two paths.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>I just reread the middle section of this thread and realized this probably falls into the nitpicking category that has been discouraged. Sorry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also that question was already answered by Neall, probably in the Ask Neall thread. You can triple-down on your Path Skills, it's just that if it pushes your Skill over 5 you have to move a dot into a different Skill associated with the Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}